# Task
This function has a bug. Find it:

function debounce(fn, ms) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    setTimeout(() => fn(...args), ms);
  };
}

pairs.output_b:
The bug: `t` is declared but never used — the previous timeout is never cancelled. Every call schedules a *new* timeout, so `fn` fires once per call instead of once per burst. That's not debouncing; it's just delaying.

Fix:
```js
function debounce(fn, ms) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), ms);
  };
}
```

